\[\frac{1}{Efficiency}\times\frac{1}{0.88}\times\frac{1}{0.64}\times 1.0027. \tag{5.1}\]

Since the rapidity range is chosen as \(|y|<0.75\), to calculate per unit rapidity the corrected values are divided by 1.5.

## Chapter 6 Experimental Findings

The corrected \(\Sigma^{*}(1385)\) and \(\overline{\Sigma^{*}}(1385)\) spectra in p+p, Au+Au  and d+Au collisions at \(\sqrt{s_{{}_{\rm NN}}}=200\) GeV collisions are presented in this chapter. The \(\Sigma^{*}(1385)\) baryon yields and \(\langle p_{T}\rangle\) dependence are extracted from the corrected spectra for various collision systems. Antiparticle to particle ratios are shown. The \(\rm p_{T}\) dependent nuclear affects are discussed in terms of the nuclear modification factor for \(\Sigma^{*}(1385)\) in d+Au and Au+Au collisions.

