The \(\rm\Theta^{+}\) pentaquark is observed to decay into two channels, n+K and \(\rm p+K^{0}_{s}\). Since there is no identification of neutrons in the TPC, the \(K^{0}_{S}+p\) decay channel is used for this search. To study the decay mechanism and to optimize the applied cuts, Monte Carlo simulations are used. For this study, first one Monte Carlo \(\rm\Theta^{+}\) pentaquark is chosen from a thermal exponential distribution with T = 300 MeV in the rapidity

