### 7.3 \(\Theta^{+}\) Pentaquark Search

A topological measurement of pentaquarks is not possible since their lifetimes are short due to their strong decay. Instead, \(\Theta^{+}\) pentaquarks are investigated using the combinatorial invariant mass technique. This is similar to the one that is used for the \(\Sigma^{*}(1385)\) resonance analysis. Three different techniques are used to minimize the backgrounds; HCT, strangeness tagging and a search using kinks.

